# What the tree of DN keeps and what it leaves to the compiler (the policy of the conditional compilation of DN OSP; see bootstrap/README.md).
# DN OSP is a Virtual Pascal project that serves several systems from one source with {$IFDEF DPMI32}, OS2, WIN32, LINUX...
# BOOT_STRIP: these symbols are taken as defined by tools/ifdef-strip.py (the branches of the other systems, OS/2 and Win32, are dropped:
#   the tree is 32-bit flat code with the long file name layer, the base of all our builds). VIRTUALPASCAL: its STDEFINE.INC takes the
#   branch of the real build (BIT_32, FILE_32, DualName, USELFN...) only when VP is defined; FPC does the job of VP here. DN and DNPRG are
#   the symbols of the command line of the original build (_dnc.cmd: vpc dn /dDN /dDNPRG): DNPRG = the program (not the plugin).
#   NOASM: the authors of DN keep Pascal versions (by Cat) of the routines that they wrote in the 32-bit Intel assembler; the tree takes them
#   (no assembler in the tree: one source for the 32-bit and the 64-bit builds; the routines that have no Pascal version are written in
#   Pascal by edits/95-asm.py and edits/99b-asm-pascal.py).
BOOT_STRIP="DPMI32 VIRTUALPASCAL DN DNPRG NOASM"
# BOOT_KEEP: the conditionals on these symbols stay in the tree: the compiler decides with -dSYMBOL (LINUX: the Linux build).
BOOT_KEEP="LINUX"
# the directory of the archive with the units of the system (DN OSP keeps the units that differ between the systems in LIB.D32, LIB.OLF, LIB.WLF)
BOOT_LIB_DIR="LIB.D32"
